ui-pf-path-crop = Crop: keep only the overlapping area of the whole selection and trim the boundaries (same geometry kernel as Intersect).
ui-pf-path-divide = Divide: all selected shapes intersect and recombine into non-overlapping atomic closed regions (open paths participate as closed); each region's fill comes from the topmost object covering it. One undo restores.
ui-pf-path-intersect = Intersect: keep only the overlapping area of the whole selection (errors when there is no overlap); style from the first-selected object.
ui-pf-path-merge = Merge: same geometry kernel as Union — in AI, merging two operands is the union; strokes/fills keep the original object styles.
ui-pf-path-outline = Outline: every edge is cut at intersections with other objects, producing unfilled open stroke lines (one per segment); strokes inherit from the source object, defaulting to 1px black when none. Self-intersections of one object are not cut.
ui-pf-path-subtract = Minus Front: keep the lower objects and subtract their overlap with the topmost (result = lower − upper, style from the lower); the rest are deleted.
ui-pf-path-subtract_back = Minus Back: the topmost object subtracts everything below it and stays (keeps the opposite object versus Minus Front).
ui-pf-path-trim = Trim: each shape subtracts the objects above it, strokes are removed, same-fill fragments merge into one; fills are kept. One undo restores.
ui-pf-path-union = Union: the selection merges into one object (union outline); the result keeps the first-selected object's style and position.
ui-pf-path-xor = Exclude: carve out every overlapping area, keeping each object's non-overlapping parts (may produce several pieces, merged into one path).
